PATCH 582: the CRT's near-hook trampoline (018a/0199 through DGROUP:0x3a), which is how the scheduler
poll steps the RNG; the task continuation's segment (3566) and its `lret` (0x1360f); the saved INT-8
vector (2ebe) as two words; the per-tick handler 5db8 and the idle handler 773e of word[0x6ce4].

board:0015 / board:0017 / board:0026.  The trap census on AZER1 after patch 581 left five targets, and
each of them was a different reading error of the same mechanism:

  018a/0199  `ff 16 3a 00` is `call [ss:0x3a]` -- a NEAR call (ModRM /2) in the trampoline's own segment
         0, not the far call [0x3c]:[0x3a] patch 073 modelled at 3920 (`push [0x310] ; ljmp [0x48]`,
         [0x48] = 0000:0199, [0x310] = 0x291): segment 0x018a (the word at [0x3c] is the 0x18a
         trampoline's OFFSET) put the target at linear 0x1b31.  [0x310] = 0x291 is the LFSR step
         FUN_0000_0291, so every scheduler poll (35ae, 38e5) advances the RNG once -- the port's RNG
         did not move there at all.  018a itself (`call [ss:0x3a] ; retf`, the [0x3c] vector) and its
         callers 1384/1394/13a4/13b4/13c4/13d4/3d07 read and wrote the slot through Ghidra's static SS
         0x2ba9 (DAT_2000_baca = 0x2baca, DAT_2000_bd02 = 0x2bd02 ..): the slot is DGROUP:0x3a, the
         sources DGROUP:0x272/0x26e/0x282/0x284/0x290/0x294/0x162c.  The hooks are 0 until installed
         and the `ret` at 0000:0000 is what a null hook runs -- emitted as FUN_0000_0000; 3835's
         constant hook 0x1c66 (`clc ; ret`) likewise.
  3566   `mov [si+0x10],cs` stored 0x1000; the oracle executes 3566 and 35a7 at 2082:3ed6 / 2082:3f17
         (the 0f69 cluster), so the continuation both arm is 0f69:3f7f = the bare `lret` at 0x1360f,
         which the next poll far-calls (135ca).  35a7 already had 0xf69 (patch 073); 3566 did not, and
         neither target existed: FUN_1000_360f is that `lret`.
  2ebe   `mov cs:[0x382a],bx ; mov cs:[0x382c],es ; mov [0x432],bx ; mov [0x434],es` after INT 21h
         AH=35: the 4-byte DAT_1000_c432 store zeroed [0x434] and Ghidra's `unaff_ES` is the ES from
         before the INT.  30f8's chain to the saved vector ([0x44b] bit 1) far-called 0000:0008 on every
         interrupt and the BIOS tick at 0040:006C never moved.  Two word stores of BX and the returned
         ES (the shim's FE00:0008), which fist_icall routes to the INT 08 service.  The shim's
         set-vector now recognises that magic as "the BIOS handler again" when the engine restores it.
  5db8   FUN_0000_4886 installs word[0x6ce4] = 0x5db8 and the main loop near-calls it once per sim tick
         (45ed); unpromoted, so the whole mode ran with its tick handler dispatching into the void.
         Transcribed from 0x5db8-0x5e5e: the 500f call, the [0x7a40]/[0x6cde] gate to 69c0, the
         [0x7a50]/[0x7ae7] countdowns, the two near state tables at 0x7d08/0x7d10 and the [0x1594]
         message with AX chosen by [0x7aea]/[0x7c52]/[0x7aec]/[0x1eb5]/[0x1f35].  72ee's idle handler
         0x773e is a bare `ret`, as c30e.

  Measured: AZER1 and TRAIN2 run to their verdicts with no trap at all (FIST_TRACE_TRAPS empty).  The
  RNG now steps once per poll, so the battles change: AZER1 DEFEAT at tick 5358 (1:29; the original's
  two runs: 5:49 and 1:38), TRAIN2 DEFEAT at 19134 (5:19; the original loses at ~4:30) -- the kind now
  agrees on both.  The original seeds its RNG from the clock and its poll count from CPU speed, so a
  tick-for-tick match with the oracle is not a property the original has with itself; native and wasm
  stay identical because the poll count is the clock model's (board:0026).

